     5	## 1. Sources and coverage
     6	
     7	**Finding.** There are nine `auto/runs/*/events.jsonl` files with 308 events and nine corresponding reports; the archived `20261025_0048_night` has `state.json` but no event/report pair (command: `glob('auto/runs/*/events.jsonl')`, count 9; `sum(lines)`, 308; `wc -l auto/runs/*/{REPORT.md,events.jsonl,state.json}`). The DB query in `OUT/scripts/audit_sessions.py:20-27` found 175 seven-character SHA sessions in its time range, of which 93 appear in saved auto run `state.json#/workers`. `OUT/POLL_STATS.csv:1` describes the full session lifetime, including time before adoption or after an auto stop; filter nonempty `auto_runs` to obtain the 93. Board results and statuses are checked by `OUT/scripts/audit_sessions.py:18-19`; `decisions.jsonl:443-450,504-505` records the relevant run overrides and stop decisions. All nine reports and event files were searched for retry, stall, doom, stop, and Docker terms; the prior S6 inventory was used as the baseline (`master_chat_work/20261030_upgrade2/S6_auto_speed/FINDINGS.md:22-35`).
