     9	**What to change / expected gain / risk / check.** Keep an immutable per-run worker index (`sha`, session ID, prompt, expected deliverable, OUT, child-job manifest) in `auto/runs/<run>/`; the current `state.json#/workers` lacks child identity and historical transition timestamps. This makes later sleep attribution exact and avoids guesswork about children. Risk: stale PID reuse; store process start time and job path, and never act on a PID alone. Check by replaying the nine saved states into a read-only audit and reconciling every `spawn`/`adopt` event to one worker row. This is a proposed morning change, not a change made here.
    10	
    11	## 2. “Went to sleep”: every identified auto episode
    12	
    13	**Finding.** `OUT/SLEEP_CASES.csv:2-11` records ten workers in two synchronized freezes. Five sessions stopped issuing tools at 23:19-23:22 and resumed at 02:50 (207-212 minutes each); another five stopped at 04:59 and resumed at 07:50 (170-172 minutes each). The first freeze is absent from the run report's stall discussion, which only names 05:00-07:50 (`auto/runs/20261027T2239_overnight/REPORT.md:5,30,80`). The event stream also has 23:14→02:53 and 04:58→07:52 delivery gaps (`auto/runs/20261027T2239_overnight/events.jsonl:19-20,47-48`). Calendar loss is about **6 h 22 m** across the two windows; summed worker idle is about **31.8 worker-hours**, and those are overlapping measures. The exact DB evidence for each worker is `SLEEP_CASES.csv#/evidence`: an assistant message `time_created` followed by a tool `state.time.start` more than 170 minutes later. The transcripts show work was incomplete: 4e298da was still writing Gate 03 of QC, 9a85fdc had a failed write then continued its fix, f0331ad was editing, and 7d4de68 was still at QC setup (`python3 OUT/scripts/timeline.py <sha> <start> <end>`; `auto/runs/20261027T2239_overnight/REPORT.md:13-14,26-30`). 361674d explicitly said, “Waiting for nop, stub, forgery” before the second gap; its Step 10 job continued (`opencode.db session.title=361674d, message.time_created=2026-10-28 04:59:10 IST, next part.state.time.start=07:50:08`).
    14	
