     3	## Defect
     4	
     5	The corpus describes twenty four semi monthly wafer start cycles at four fabrication sites and asks for an apportionment of scarce capacity, yet the evidence that fixes every input to that apportionment is spread across forty two record and declaration files written by thirteen different systems, and several of those systems disagree. The work is wrong in a believable way unless each of the following is handled.
     6	
     7	1. (focal) The shared fill level. Capacity is handed out by raising one level across every claiming request of a site cycle after the committed minimums are paid, so the grant of any request depends on the claims of all the others in that cell. The habitual reading, sharing capacity in proportion to the quantities asked for, is written down in `legacy_runbook.md` and is withdrawn. Defeats `region_ledger_backbone_exact` and `site_cycle_capacity_and_fill_exact`.
     8	2. (focal) The carried shortfall. An unmet claim becomes a lot that attaches to the same identity and site, survives a withheld number of cycles, is cut before the current quantity when a ceiling binds, is discharged oldest first when a grant arrives, and is cleared outright at a site whose cycle ends with capacity unused. The running totals never heal, so one wrong decision at cycle five is still visible at cycle twenty four. Defeats `cumulative_shortfall_spine_exact`.
     9	3. (focal) The two withheld rules. Neither the governor of quantity before the July cutover nor the survival age of a carried lot is stated anywhere in the contract. Each has to be settled by testing the candidate readings against a settlement log, and the surviving reading has to be reported in `policy_audit.json`. A guess that fits part of the log is wrong. Defeats the backbone checks and judge criteria R9 and R10.
    10	4. (drift) The single conversion stage. `rounding_rules.md` section 2 describes a conversion that rounds at every substitution hop; `errata_2031-07.md` replaces that section with one conversion for the whole walk. Rounding per hop moves a small share of rows by one wafer equivalent and nothing else, which looks like a clean result. Defeats `substitution_served_node_and_hops_exact` and `granted_wafers_truncation_exact`.
    11	5. (drift) The duplicate column title. Every order book part carries two columns titled `quantity`. The first governs. A dictionary reader keeps the second, which agrees with the first on roughly four rows in five. Defeats the backbone checks through the governing quantity.
    12	6. (trap) Admission by recorded instant. Rows recorded after `2032-01-10T00:00:00Z` are evidence of nothing, including capacity revisions, ceilings, exceptions, state events and amendment notices. Defeats `data_quality_source_counts_exact` and the backbone.
    13	7. (trap) Identity across epochs. A reused customer identifier carries two epochs with different segments, and the two epochs share no ceiling, no commitment and no carried lot. Defeats `segment_rollups_exact` and `cross_artifact_identity_triangle_holds`.
    14	8. (trap) The substitution walk. A request for an unqualified node walks the cheapest edge in force at the cycle start, at most three hops, and two nodes close a cycle between them. The shortest path to any qualified node is a different answer. Defeats `substitution_served_node_and_hops_exact`.
