+VERDICT: The six completed learning sessions support immediate QC template corrections, better job observability, narrow Docker housekeeping, and a design-only hidden-case pilot.
+
+## 1. Session coverage and evidence
+
+**Finding.** L1-L6 each contain `FINDINGS.md`, `QUESTIONS.md`, extras, and a `DONE` result; none is missing or PARTIAL. `python3 scripts/audit_synthesis.py` prints six `DONE` statuses and the main CSV counts (585 QC findings, 303 kit rows, 93 auto-linked sessions, 552 image rows). The read-only primary spot checks in [LEARNING_REPORT.md](LEARNING_REPORT.md) section “Ten source spot-checks” are 10 RIGHT, 0 WRONG. **Change where:** preserve the source-linked report in L7 OUT for morning review. **Expected gain:** one audit trail across sessions. **Could break:** snapshots age and derived CSV counts can hide source interpretation errors. **Check:** rerun [audit script](scripts/audit_synthesis.py) and the ten named primary-source reads.
+
+## 2. Ranked lessons and changes
+
+**Finding.** The live kit requires five fresh 1.000 oracle runs and permits small justified artifact-presence credit; P2/P12 currently say three runs and any pass fails ([kit](../../../Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md):354-390,418-420; [P2](../../../master_chat_tasks/prompts/templates/P2_build_v5.md):132,137; [P12](../../../master_chat_tasks/prompts/templates/P12_recheck_fix_v4.md):62,67). L1 indexes 27 temporal fix/new-finding links, and the kit demands a graded trigger for every rule ([L1](../L1_qc_fixes/FINDINGS.md):15-25; [AL-27](../../../Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/05_Alignment_Integrity_QC.md):38). **Change where:** tomorrow, correct P2/P12 final-QC targets, decide the house vacuity rule, then add a touched-rule/observable receipt to the playbook. **Expected gain:** kit-complete sign-off and fewer recurrent rule/prose defects; latter gain INFERRED. **Could break:** extra QC time and check-count growth. **Check:** five distinct frozen-copy oracle results, priced stub/forgery, one-rule mutants, and DS-22/TS-23/CL-4 review. Full ranking is in [LEARNING_REPORT.md](LEARNING_REPORT.md) sections “Ranked changes”.
+
+## 3. Auto mode and Docker
+
+**Finding.** L3 reports two synchronized worker freezes and 987 sleep calls across 93 auto-linked sessions, but the shared-freeze root layer and recoverable wall time are UNVERIFIED ([L3](../L3_auto_problems/FINDINGS.md):11-31; `python3 scripts/audit_synthesis.py` output). L4's saved snapshot contains 552 image rows and 18.73 GB of Buildx cache accounting, not a current deletion target ([images](../L4_docker/IMAGES.csv); [Buildx](../L4_docker/inventory/buildx_du_verbose.txt):7914-7917). **Change where:** add job manifests, bounded completion waits, per-worker progress alerts and a dry-run watchdog in `auto.py`/worker rules; later test CPU/memory admission and targeted idle cleanup. **Expected gain:** faster detection and fewer model polls; wall and physical-disk gains UNVERIFIED. **Could break:** false alerts, duplicate jobs, OOM, cold builds. **Check:** replay L3 episodes and fake job outcomes, then controlled Docker admission and before/after inventory tests after active work ends ([L3](../L3_auto_problems/FINDINGS.md):37-49; [L4](../L4_docker/CLEANUP.md):1-61).
+
+## 4. Task design and conflicts
+
+**Finding.** L5's lowest recorded Opus scores are not proof of QC-safe design: foundry's truth calls two graded rules withheld, and royalty's scenario hash collapses nine reports ([foundry](../../../anubis-stage-2/aa314fee-a873-5778-9d55-e8892e6d7cda/solution/TRUTH.md):7-9; [royalty](../../../anubis-stage-2/75407a55-6665-505e-95d8-5ff9bdb3384f/tests/test_output.py):74-115). L6's rolling-reservations score chance is explicitly INFERRED ([ideas](../L6_web_ideas/IDEAS.md):1-7). L1's 14 DS-22 tasks and L2's 11 DS-22 fail tasks use different severity filters, so they do not conflict ([L1](../L1_qc_fixes/FINDINGS.md):21-25; [L2](../L2_qc_kit_map/FINDINGS.md):7-11). **Change where:** select a design-only pilot, require a determinate contract and uniqueness proof in `LEVER_RULES_v3.md`, and prefer meaningful per-field/report credit in future tests. **Expected gain:** avoid full builds of easy or unfair ideas; gain INFERRED. **Could break:** a strict early screen can reject a viable task, and fairer credit may raise final score. **Check:** independent oracle, three valid hidden seeds, generic solver, one-fact score perturbation, and full QC before any frozen paid run ([lever rules](../../../master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md):227-244; [CL-4](../../../Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md):491).
+
+No task, template, auto code, Docker image or process was changed. The six material UNVERIFIED items are listed at the end of [LEARNING_REPORT.md](LEARNING_REPORT.md).
