+# Decisions for Ayush
+
+The live QC kit already settles the five-oracle-run requirement, so that correction is in the report rather than here ([kit](../../../Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md):354-390; [P2](../../../master_chat_tasks/prompts/templates/P2_build_v5.md):132).
+
+1. **Should the house vacuity rule fail every positive stub score?** Recommended: follow the live kit. Allow small, justified artifact-presence credit; fail content-blind checks or a forgery that earns genuine-partial credit. Option: keep “any pass = fail” as a stricter house rule, labelled as such. Evidence: [kit](../../../Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md):418-420,489; [P2](../../../master_chat_tasks/prompts/templates/P2_build_v5.md):137.
+2. **When `auto.py stop --now` finds a verified child job still running, what should it do?** Recommended: leave it running and report its PID/start time, log, input tree and expected result; stop children only on an explicit request. Option: stop verified children automatically. Evidence: [L3](../L3_auto_problems/QUESTIONS.md):3.
+3. **Should an independent watchdog watch `auto.py` itself?** Recommended: yes, after a dry run proves one leader and no duplicate sends. Option: use `check_gap` only, which reports after `auto.py` resumes. Evidence: [L3](../L3_auto_problems/QUESTIONS.md):5; [auto.py](../../../master_chat_tasks/auto/auto.py):1712-1718.
+4. **How much BuildKit cache should remain after a later idle-window cleanup?** Recommended: 15 GB. Option: 10 GB if disk pressure outweighs the cold-build risk. Snapshot accounting was 18.73 GB; actual host savings are UNVERIFIED. Evidence: [L4](../L4_docker/QUESTIONS.md):1-7; [Buildx snapshot](../L4_docker/inventory/buildx_du_verbose.txt):7914-7917.
+5. **Which idea should get the next design-only pilot?** Recommended: rolling reservations with a stated state-transition contract and three valid hidden seeds. Option: parametric network repair if it better fits the live task portfolio. Neither has a verified score forecast. Evidence: [L6](../L6_web_ideas/IDEAS.md):5-13,20-23; [L5 copy rules](../L5_stage2_study/PATTERNS.md):23-27.
+6. **Should house scoring usually award per-field or per-report credit even when exact output is allowed?** Recommended: yes, except when one whole object is the natural correctness unit; check one-fact score before freezing. Option: use the kit's explicit exact-match exception as written. Evidence: [CL-4](../../../Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md):491; [L5](../L5_stage2_study/QUESTIONS.md):4.
